From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: A frame sent in part is reported and counted

juice_send_batch returns how many datagrams the socket took. After its bounded wait for a full socket buffer that
can be fewer than it was given, and IceTransport::sendBatch took any count as success, so a frame missing its last
packets looked sent: nothing reached the sender's own counters, and the missing datagrams never reach the queue or
the interface counters either. The batch is now a success only when every datagram was taken; the others are
counted (UnsentMediaDatagrams) where the number is known. DtlsSrtpTransport keeps that result when an RTCP packet
follows the frame, and Track::sendFrame returns it. What the socket took is not sent again.
